does define __cpp_lib_to_chars 201611L. I'm fairly confident (libc++ has defined it since ~LLVM 8). So the comment "libc++ does not define __cpp_lib_to_chars" is factually wrong, and the #else branch is dead on macOS. On macOS 26 SDK with availability — FP from_chars is marked availability macOS 26 → using it with a lower deployment target gives a compile error (or weak-link). So: macOS builds with older SDK/deployment target break at compile time. And the project CI's macOS build presumably passes because the runner is new. Report as finding with fix: explicitly test `!defined(_LIBCPP_VERSION)` (or a dedicated configure check) for the FP from_chars path, and keep istringstream for libc++.

